course: dictionary
lesson: 9081
title: One word, several jobs
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do more than one job, and the words around them show which job they are doing. Slouch can be a verb (something you do) or a noun (a thing you have). Context clues tell you which one it is.
explain: «She sat slouched over her desk, her head hanging forward.» Here slouched is a verb: she is sitting with rounded shoulders in a lazy, droopy way. Try your meaning in the sentence. Does "sat with a droopy back" still make sense? Yes, so you have it.
explain: «Her slouch made her look tired.» Now slouch is a noun: it is the droopy way of sitting. In «Maya is no slouch at maths», the words "no slouch" mean something else again. Read the words around it before you decide.
fact: To slouch is to sit, stand or walk with your shoulders rounded and your head hanging forward.
fact: A slouch is that droopy way of sitting or standing.
fact: "No slouch" is informal and means very good at something.
fact: «Slouching for a while does no harm», but sitting in one position for hours does, so get up, stretch and move often.
fact: A slouch hat is a soft hat with a wide brim, famous in Australian army uniform.
exercise: «She sat and slouched over her phone all afternoon.» What is slouched doing here? | Running fast | Standing up very tall | Singing loudly | *Sitting with rounded shoulders and head hanging forward
exercise: Ben says, «Maya is no slouch at maths.» What does no slouch mean? | Maya hates maths | Maya is lazy about maths | Maya is slow at reading | *Maya is very good at maths
exercise: «Stop slouching and sit up straight, Sam!» Which advice is best? | Slouch more at your desk | *Sit up with your back supported | Lie down on the floor | Hunch over your phone for hours
test: In «Her slouch made her look tired», is slouch a noun or a verb? | Adjective | Adverb | *Noun | Verb
test: What is a slouch hat? | A tiny hat for a doll | A helmet made of metal | A hat you wear in the water | *A soft hat with a wide brim
exam: According to «Slouching for a while does no harm», is slouching for a while dangerous? | Yes, it always gives you a hunchback | No, and sitting for hours is always fine | *No, but sitting in one position for hours can do harm | Yes, it makes your muscles stronger
